 34S     31P(A,PG)                     1970MO09,1971MU03,1972JO10ENSDF    202609
 34S   H TYP=FUL$AUT=LIJIE SUN AND JUN CHEN$CIT=ENSDF$CUT=30-Sep-2026$          
 34S   H TYP=FUL$AUT=NINEL NICA, BALRAJ SINGH$CIT=NDS 113, 1563 (2012)$         
 34S 2 H CUT=28-May-2012$                                                       

 34S  c  1971Mu03: E=11.0-MeV |a beam was provided from the University of       
 34S 2c  Liverpool tandem accelerator and bombarded a natural red phosphorus    
 34S 3c  target on a C backing. Protons were detected using an annular silicon  
 34S 4c  surface-barrier detector. |g rays were detected using an array of five 
 34S 5c  NaI(Tl) detectors. Measured E{-p}, I{-p}, E|g, I|g, p|g-coin, and      
 34S 6c  p|g(|q). Deduced levels, J, |p, |g branching ratios, multipolarities,  
 34S 7c  and multipole mixing ratios.                                           

 34S  c  1970Mo09: E=8.0-MeV |a beam was provided from the Triangle Universities
 34S 2c  Nuclear Laboratory 4 MV Van de Graaff accelerator and bombarded a      
 34S 3c  target of 200-|mg/cm2 Zn{-3}P{-2} evaporated onto a 20-|mg/cm2 C       
 34S 4c  backing. Protons were detected using a 100-|mm annular silicon         
 34S 5c  surface-barrier detector. |g rays were detected using a NaI(Tl)        
 34S 6c  detector and 20-cm3 coaxial Ge(Li) detector. Measured E{-p}, I{-p},    
 34S 7c  E|g, I|g, p|g-coin, and p|g(|q). Deduced levels, J, |p,                
 34S 8c  multipolarities, and multipole mixing ratios. Also measured            
 34S 9c  {+31}P(|a,n|g){+34}Cl and {+34}Cl isomer decay.                        

 34S  c  1970Gr11: E=6-9 MeV |a beams were provided from the University of      
 34S 2c  Liverpool EN tandem accelerator and bombarded a natural red phosphorus 
 34S 3c  target on an Au backing. |g rays were detected using a a Ge(Li)-NaI(T1)
 34S 4c  anti-Compton and pair escape spectrometer. Measured E|g, I|g. Deduced  
 34S 5c  levels, |g branching ratios, and lifetimes using DSAM.                 

 34S  c  1970Ra17: E=5.0-7.3 MeV |a beams were provided from the Triangle       
 34S 2c  Universities Nuclear Laboratory (TUNL) FN Van de Graaff accelerator and
 34S 3c  bombarded a target of gallium phosphide (GaP) on a Ni backing. |g rays 
 34S 4c  were detected using a Ge(Li) coaxial detector. Measured E|g, I|g.      
 34S 5c  Deduced lifetimes using DSAM.                                          

 34S  c  1972Jo10: E=9.3 and 11.0 MeV |a beams were provided from the University
 34S 2c  of Liverpool tandem accelerator and bombarded a target of red          
 34S 3c  phosphorus on a C backing. Protons were detected using an annular      
 34S 4c  silicon surface-barrier detector. |g rays were detected using five     
 34S 5c  NaI(Tl) detectors, one Ge(Li) detector, or five Ge(Li) detectors.      
 34S 6c  Measured E{-p}, I{-p}, E|g, I|g, p|g-coin, and p|g(|q). Deduced levels,
 34S 7c  J, |p, |g branching ratios, multipolarities, and multipole mixing      
 34S 8c  ratios.                                                                

 34S  c  1974Gr06: E=7.2-8.0, 10.8, 11.0 MeV |a beams were provided from the    
 34S 2c  University of Freiburg 7 MV Van de Graaff accelerator and bombarded a  
 34S 3c  target of Zn{-3}P{-2} on a Ta or Ni backing. Protons were detected     
 34S 4c  using an annular silicon surface-barrier detector. |g rays were        
 34S 5c  detected using a Ge(Li) detector or two NaI(Tl) detectors. Measured    
 34S 6c  E{-p}, I{-p}, E|g, I|g, p|g-coin, |g|g-coin, and p|g(|q). Deduced      
 34S 7c  levels, J, |p, |g branching ratios, multipolarities, multipole mixing  
 34S 8c  ratios, and lifetimes from DSAM lineshape analysis. 1977GrZH: an       
 34S 9c  abstract by the same group of 1974Gr06 using E{-|a}=13.9 MeV at        
 34S Ac  University of Freiburg. Measured higher-lying levels. 1969Gr03:        
 34S Bc  E{-|a}=5.90 MeV at University of Freiburg. Measured lifetimes of two   
 34S Cc  34S levels from DSAM lineshape analysis.                               

 34S  c  1970Br18: E=4.67-MeV |a beam from the 5.5 MV Van de Graaff generator at
 34S 2c  the National Laboratory of Legnaro, Padova. Targets were red phosphorus
 34S 3c  on C foils. Deduced lifetimes of two 34S levels using DSAM.            

 34S  c  1970Cu02: E=8.05, 8.14, 8.35 MeV |a beams from the Atomic Energy       
 34S 2c  Research Establishment (AERE), UK. Targets were red phosphorus on Ni   
 34S 3c  and Ti backings foils Ni foils. Protons were detected using an annular 
 34S 4c  silicon surface-barrier detector. |g rays were detected using a NaI(Tl)
 34S 5c  detector and a Ge(Li) detector. Deduced lifetimes of two 34S levels    
 34S 6c  from DSAM lineshape analysis.                                          

 34S  c  1971Gr26: E=9.5 MeV |a beam bombarded a target of red phosphorus on a  
 34S 2c  Au backing. |g rays were detected using a single planar Ge(Li)         
 34S 3c  polarimeter and a Ge(Li) detector. Measured E|g, I|g, |g(|q), and      
 34S 4c  linear polarization. Deduced the level at 5.689 MeV has J|p=5- and its 
 34S 5c  deexcitation |g multipolarities and multipole mixing ratios.           

 34S  c  1972Gr15: E=9.5 MeV |a beam was provided from the Chalk River MP tandem
 34S 2c  accelerator and bombarded a target of InP on a stretched Au backing. |g
 34S 3c  rays were detected using a Ge(Li) detector. Deduced the lifetime of the
 34S 4c  5.689-MeV level using the recoil-distance Doppler-shift method.        

 34S  c  1979Ba54: E=6.30 and 7.00 MeV |a beams were provided from the Frankfurt
 34S 2c  7.5 MV Van de Graaff accelerator. |g rays were detected using four     
 34S 3c  cylindrical $Ge(Li)$ detectors. Measured E|g, I|g, |g(|q), and         
 34S 4c  polarization sensitivity. Deduced multipolarities and multipole mixing 
 34S 5c  ratios.                                                                

 34S  c  1988Mc05: {+31}P(|a,p) with E=1.7-5.5 MeV |a beams from the 5.5-MV CN  
 34S 2c  Van de Graaff accelerator at the University of Arizona. Measured proton
 34S 3c  yields.                                                                

 34S  c  1975So11: {+31}P(|a,p) with E=7.60 MeV |a beam from the 5.5-MV Van de  
 34S 2c  Graaff accelerator at Louis Pasteur University, Strasbourg, France. The
 34S 3c  target was red phosphorus on Au backings. Protons were detected using a
 34S 4c  300-|mm thick silicon surface-barrier annular counter.                 
 34S 5c  Electron-positron pairs were detected using a |DE-E telescope of       
 34S 6c  plastic scintillators. Deduced E0 pair branching ratios.               

 34S  c  1962Li07: {+31}P(|a,p) with E=42 MeV |a beam from the University of    
 34S 2c  Washington cyclotron. The target was red phosphorus on polystyrene     
 34S 3c  backings. Protons were detected using a |DE-E telescope of plastic and 
 34S 4c  CsI(Tl) detectors. Measured |s(E{-p},|q).                              

